Package: quadrf-lora-phy
Architecture: arm64
Conflicts: quadrf-phy
Replaces: quadrf-phy
Provides: quadrf-phy
Depends:
 bluez,
 bluez-firmware,
 python3,
 python3-dbus,
 python3-gi,
 quadrf-fpga (>= 1.0.0),
 quadrf-soapy (>= 1.0.1),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: experimental QuadRF LoRa-compatible PHY daemon
 Owns the QuadRF SoapySDR/FPGA front end and chirp-spread-spectrum modem,
 then exposes Meshtastic air frames and receive metadata through Air-IPC v1
 at /run/quadrf/phy.sock.
 .
 This independent experimental package is not an official Scale RF or
 Meshtastic product or support channel.

Package: quadrf-meshtasticd
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 openssl,
 quadrf-lora-phy (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: python3-meshtastic, xdg-utils
Description: experimental Meshtastic daemon with QuadRF Air-IPC adapter
 Provides a Meshtastic-derived native daemon, the out-of-tree QuadRF
 RadioInterface adapter, and a checksum-locked Meshtastic Web client. It
 communicates with quadrf-lora-phy over /run/quadrf/phy.sock and packages the
 out-of-tree QuadRF backend adapter.
 The package registers a QuadRF desktop entry and control-page application.
 .
 This independent experimental package is not an official Scale RF or
 Meshtastic product or support channel.

Package: quadrf-mesh
Architecture: all
Depends:
